          "cwe_id": "CWE-141",
          "name": "Improper Neutralization of Parameter/Argument Delimiters"
        }
      ],
      "description": "### Summary\r\n\r\n`Plug.Conn.Cookies.encode/2` in the Elixir `plug` library builds the `Set-Cookie` response header by interpolating the cookie `path`, `domain` and `same_site` attributes directly into the header string without validating the `;` character. Any Plug application that reflects attacker-controlled data into a cookie attribute lets an unauthenticated attacker inject additional cookie attributes through `;`. Plug already handles `\\r\\n` and null bytes accordingly, so header injection is not possible.\r\n\r\n### Impact\r\n\r\nAn unauthenticated attacker whose input is reflected into a cookie can inject arbitrary cookie attributes. Every Plug-based application that places untrusted data into a cookie attribute is affected, they must either upgrade their Plug version or ensure the untrusted data does not have the `;` character in it.\r\n\r\n### References\r\n\r\n* Introduction commit: https://github.com/elixir-plug/plug/commit/f26876aa67aaeb38e616638aa3efbcc2fe2906a5\r\n* Patch commit: https://github.com/elixir-plug/plug/commit/c6575800b2c4e15af1904df87522ca8a23da020c\r\n",
